diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c4bd3a9..68b5759 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -827,6 +827,21 @@ stream describes a target or pet with only a name and an HP per-mille value.
 
 `target_id` and `pet_id` are omitted entirely when there is no target or no pet.
 
+#### Target of target
+The `player` message also carries the assist candidate for your current target,
+from the same sources `/assistbar` draws from (see that command):
+
+- `target_of_target` - who your target last hit (assist semantics)
+- `target_hit_by` - who last hit your target (defend semantics)
+
+Each is an object `{ "id": <spawn id>, "name": "<name>", "authoritative": <bool> }`.
+`authoritative` is true when the value came from the server's reply to `/assist`
+(which requires the bar to be enabled, though it need not be visible) and false
+when it was inferred from damage packets. `name` is omitted when the entity is
+gone or a corpse; each key is omitted when there is no fresh candidate. Damage
+inference runs whenever a pipe client is attached, so the bar does not have to
+be turned on for these to appear.
+
 ---
